# Void — Development Rules

## Workflow

- Use void-mcp tools to inspect Grok's live code. Don't guess module structure.
- Run `bun run lint:fix`, `bun run lint:styles:fix`, `bun run tsc` after changes. Don't run `bun run build` unless asked.
- After building, remind user to reload the extension and restart MCP (`bun run mcp`).
- Fix with the smallest possible change. No refactoring unless asked.
- Don't add finders/utils/components to `turbopack/common/` unless existing code already needs them.
- Push back when the user's idea is wrong or misguided.

## Code Style

Write modern, clean, professional code. Every function should be the shortest correct version of itself — same functionality, less code, always. If you can remove a line and behavior stays the same, remove it. Prefer the simplest approach that handles all cases properly.

- **Robust**: every code path returns a value or handles the case. No empty blocks, no silent failures, no unhandled edge cases. Catch blocks must do something (log, return, rethrow).
- **Fast**: no unnecessary re-renders, no API spam (debounce/cache where needed), no redundant computation. `Promise.all` for parallel async. `.find`/`.some` over `.filter()[0]`.
- **Organized**: file order is imports → Logger → finders → types → constants → functions/components → definePlugin export. Group related logic together.
- **Concise**: inline single-use variables unless they clarify intent. No wrapper functions that just call another function. No redundant type annotations the compiler infers. No unnecessary destructuring.
- **DRY**: no duplicate logic across files. If two files share the same helper, extract it to a shared location or re-export. When a pattern repeats (e.g. read-modify-write on settings), extract a shared helper in the same file.

### What NOT to do

- **No single-use wrappers**: if a function is 1–3 lines and called once, inline it at the call site.
- **No trivial getters/setters**: `getX() { return this.x; }` — access the value directly.
- **No alias re-exports**: don't create `camelToTitle` that just calls `humanizeKey`. Import the original.
- **No falsy-value JSX gates**: `{arr.length && <Foo/>}` renders `0` when empty. Use `{!!arr.length && <Foo/>}` or `{arr.length > 0 && <Foo/>}`.
- **No mutation before spread**: `const obj = existing ?? {}; obj.key = val; save({...base, obj})` mutates the original. Always copy first: `const obj = {...(existing ?? {})}`.
- **No dangling subscriptions**: every `subscribe()` must have a matching `unsubscribe()` in all code paths (success, error, early return).
- **No `map` returning nulls**: use `.filter().map()` instead of `.map(x => cond ? <X/> : null)`.
- **No manual patterns when utils exist**: use `onlyOnce()` instead of hand-rolled `fired` flags, `createExternalStore()` instead of manual subscribe/getSnapshot, shared helpers instead of repeated spread patterns.
- **No barrel imports for submodules**: import from `@turbopack/common/utils`, not `@turbopack/common`.

### What TO do

- Inline trivial helpers at their single call site.
- Extract repeated multi-line patterns into a local helper within the same file.
- Use `filter().map()` for conditional rendering lists.
- Copy objects before mutating: `const copy = {...original}; copy.key = val;`.
- Clean up all subscriptions and timers in every exit path.
- Use existing utilities from `@utils/*` — check what's available before writing manual logic.
- Prefer `for...of` with a counter over double-pass `.filter().length` when you need both count and iteration.

- License header on new files uses 2026. Never edit existing headers.
- No comments unless explicitly asked. Keep existing ones.
- Delete dead code, don't comment it out.
- Descriptions: capital first letter, end with period.
- Write natural human text in errors, descriptions, messages.
- Guard clause and return early. Never nest 3+ levels deep.
- Use `Logger` from `@utils/Logger`. Never raw `console.log/warn/error`.
- Prefer optional chaining, nullish coalescing, `const`, arrow functions, `satisfies` over `as`.
- Trust type inference for locals. Annotate exports and params.
- Use `any` over `unknown` when something can't be properly typed. Use proper types from `packages/grok-types/` for Grok objects.
- Use enum types from `packages/grok-types/enums/` instead of raw string/number literals. Patch strings are exempt.
- Empty catch blocks are forbidden (except turbopack module iteration).
- Never nest ternaries. Use early returns or variables.
- Never mutate function parameters.

## Imports

Always use centralized imports. Never create per-file finders for things that exist in common modules.

| Need | Import from |
|------|-------------|
| React, hooks, Fragment, ReactDOM | `@turbopack/common/react` |
| Grok components (Button, Dialog, etc.) | `@turbopack/common/components` or `@components` |
| Zustand stores | `@turbopack/common/stores` |
| ApiClients, Toaster, ClassNames, i18n, NextRouter, TanStackQuery, FileUtils, CopyUtils, etc. | `@turbopack/common/utils` |
| isTruthy, isNonNullish, isObject | `@utils/guards` |
| humanizeKey, pluralize, escapeRegExp | `@utils/text` |
| useForceUpdater, useFiltered, useCountdown, useEventSubscription | `@utils/react` |
| copyToClipboard, debounce, sleep, clamp, errorMessage, sanitizeFilename, formatCountdown, formatDuration, mergeDefaults, onlyOnce, fetchExternal, createExternalStore | `@utils/misc` |
| registerStyle, enableStyle, disableStyle, classNameFactory, classes | `@utils/css` |
| Logger | `@utils/Logger` |
| addTheme, removeTheme, enableTheme, disableTheme, getThemes, isThemesEnabled, setThemesEnabled | `@api/Themes` |
| ConfirmDialog, ErrorBoundary, ErrorCard | `@components` |
| Text, Flex, Grid, Paragraph, Chip, ChatBarButton | `@components` |
| Icons | `@components/icons` |

## Components

### Void Components

| Component | Use for | Key props |
|-----------|---------|-----------|
| `Text` | Styled text spans/blocks | `as` (default `"div"`), `size` (xs/sm/base/lg/xl/2xl), `weight` (normal/medium/semibold/bold), `color` (primary/secondary/muted) |
| `Paragraph` | Short helper/description text | `color` (primary/secondary/muted). Renders `<p>` with `text-xs text-pretty`. |
| `Flex` | Flexbox layout | `flexDirection`, `gap` (default `"1em"`), `justifyContent`, `alignItems`, `flexWrap` |
| `Grid` | Grid layout | `columns`, `rows`, `gap` (default `"0.75rem"`), `justifyItems`, `alignItems` |
| `Chip` | Badge/tag labels | `variant` (default/secondary/destructive/outline) |
| `ChatBarButton` | Buttons next to chat input | `icon`, `tooltip`, `children` (label text), `iconOnly` |
| `ConfirmDialog` | Confirm/cancel prompts | `open`, `onOpenChange`, `title`, `description`, `onConfirm`, `danger` |
| `ErrorBoundary` | Wrap risky components | `.wrap(Component, fallback?)` static method for inline wrapping |
| `ErrorCard` | Error state display | `title`, `children` |

### When to use what

- **Flex/Grid** for layout containers. Plain `<div>` is fine for simple wrappers.
- **Text** for titles, labels, and inline text that needs size/weight/color control. Use `as="span"` for inline.
- **Paragraph** for ALL description/helper text — under section headings, empty states, settings descriptions, plugin info. Never use `<Text size="xs" color="secondary">` for descriptions — use `<Paragraph>` instead.
- **Chip** for small labels/badges.
- Plain `<span>`/`<div>` with Tailwind classes are fine for trivial cases.
- No inline `style={{}}` unless dynamic computed values or layout component internals.

### Section header pattern

Use this pattern for section titles with descriptions in settings/tabs:

```tsx
<Flex flexDirection="column" gap="0">
    <Text size="sm" weight="medium">Section Title</Text>
    <Paragraph>Description text explaining what this section does.</Paragraph>
</Flex>
```

Never use `<Text size="xs" color="secondary">` for the description line. Always `<Paragraph>`.

### Grok Components (from `@turbopack/common/components`)

Button, ButtonWithTooltip, Dialog/DialogContent/DialogHeader/DialogTitle/DialogFooter/DialogClose, DropdownMenu family, ContextMenu family, Select family, Popover family, Tabs family, Accordion family, Command family, Card, Input, Textarea, Switch, Checkbox, Slider, Separator, Skeleton, Spinner, Avatar, Tooltip/TooltipTrigger/TooltipContent, MotionDiv, AnimatePresence, SettingsRow/SettingsTitle/SettingsDescription, toast.

## CSS

- `classNameFactory("void-foo-")` — prefix must end with `-`. Use `cl("bar")` not `cl("-bar")`.
- Only use `cl()` for our own CSS class names. Never use Tailwind utility classes in Void code — always write proper CSS in `styles.css`.
- `classes(cl("foo"), cl("bar"))` to combine. Never template strings like `` `${a} ${b}` ``.
- Plugin CSS files are always named `styles.css`.
- `registerStyle(name, css)` for runtime CSS injection.

## Plugin Structure

```
src/plugins/<name>/index.ts(x)    — entry, uses definePlugin
src/plugins/<name>/styles.css     — optional CSS
```

Folder suffixes: `.dev` (dev builds only), `.chrome` (Chromium only). Load order: `_core/` then `_api/` then regular.

### definePlugin shape

```typescript
export default definePlugin({
    name: "PluginName",
    description: "What it does.",
    authors: [Devs.Prism],
    settings,                          // from definePluginSettings()

    // Lifecycle
    start() {},
    stop() {},

    // Patch helpers (called via $self._method() from patches)
    _helperMethod() {},

    // Extension points
    patches: [],
    chatBarButton: { render: Component },
    contextMenuItems: { conversation: { label, render } },
    managedStyle: "style-name",        // auto enable/disable with plugin
    events: { eventName: handler },
    startAt: "TurbopackReady",         // "Init" (default), "DOMContentLoaded", "TurbopackReady"
});
```

### Settings

```typescript
const settings = definePluginSettings({
    optionName: {
        type: OptionType.BOOLEAN,
        description: "What this does.",
        default: true,
    },
});
```

Types: `BOOLEAN`, `STRING`, `NUMBER`, `SELECT`, `SLIDER`, `COMPONENT`.

## Patching

### Tokens

| Token | Expands to | Use |
|-------|-----------|-----|
| `\i` | `(?:[A-Za-z_$][\w$]*)` | Any minified identifier |
| `$self` | `Void.plugins["Name"]` | Call back into plugin from patched code |
| `$&` | Entire match | Append/prepend without capture groups |
| `$1`, `$2` | Capture groups | Reuse captured content in replace |
| `.{0,N}` | Bounded gap | Bridge variable-length sections. Set N to ~1.5x actual. |

### Rules

- Every `find` must match exactly 1 module (or shared factory group). Verify with MCP.
- Good `find` anchors: i18n keys, displayName strings, feature flags, prop names.
- Every `match` regex must contain a stable string literal. Pure `\i` chains break on updates.
- Use `$&` to append/prepend. Only use capture groups when reusing content.
- Use `group: true` for multi-step transforms instead of one massive regex.
- Use `all: true` for shared factories (multiple module IDs, same source).
- Use `noWarn: true` when a patch legitimately may not match (conditional features).
- Always test patches with MCP `patch test` before finalizing.
- `find` must be as close as possible to where `match` hits. Minimize scan distance — pick anchors near the replacement site, not across the module.
- Minimize `\i` count. Use bounded `.{0,N}` gaps or more literal text instead of chaining `\i` wildcards.

### Never

- Hardcode minified names (`e`, `t`, `n`) — use `\i`.
- Use `.*?` or `.+?` — use `.{0,N}` with a bounded length.
- Write pure identifier patterns like `/\i\|\|\i/` alone — pair with a string anchor.
- Write massive regex — split into `group: true` replacements.
- Reassemble deeply nested brackets — match up to an anchor, use `$&`.

## Project Structure

```
src/api/            — logic, state, registries (no patches, no UI)
src/components/     — Void custom components + icons
src/plugins/_core/  — core patches that inject API functionality
src/plugins/_api/   — API injection patches
src/plugins/        — user-facing plugins
src/turbopack/      — module system, patching engine, common exports
src/turbopack/common/
    components.ts   — Grok component wrappers (LazyComponent + findExportedComponent)
    stores.ts       — Grok Zustand store finders (38 stores)
    utils.ts        — Grok utility finders (ApiClients, i18n, NextRouter, etc.)
    react.tsx       — React instance, hooks, Fragment, ReactDOM
packages/grok-types/
    components.d.ts — type definitions for Grok components
    stores/         — type definitions for Grok stores
    enums/          — string/number literal union types (18 files, 65+ unions)
```

### Adding Grok internals

- **New component**: type in `grok-types/components.d.ts` → `LazyComponent` in `common/components.ts`
- **New store**: interface in `grok-types/stores/` → typed finder in `common/stores.ts`
- **New util**: typed finder in `common/utils.ts`
- **New enum**: type union in `grok-types/enums/` → re-export from barrel

Only add when existing code actually needs it. Don't add speculatively.

## Settings Tabs

- Wrapper div handles `flex-1`, `w-full`, `h-full`, padding, `overflow-scroll`.
- Tab components never set width/height/overflow/flex:1 or create inner scroll containers.
- Root element: bare `<Flex flexDirection="column" gap="...">`.
- Verify appearance against Grok's native settings using MCP tools.
